<title>KAZAKHSTAN: Kazakh 3-mth T-bill av yield rises to 10.64 pct.</title>
<headline>Kazakh 3-mth T-bill av yield rises to 10.64 pct.</headline>
<dateline>ALMATY 1997-06-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>The average yield on an issue of three-month MKM discount Treasury bills rose to 10.64 percent annual at an auction on Tuesday from 10.30 percent at the last auction on June 3, the National Bank said. Details of the auction:</p>
<p>					   June 10	    June 3</p>
<p> Series number			 KZ43K1109976     KZ43K0409971</p>
<p> Issue volume (million tenge)	  600		  500</p>
<p> Bids (nominal, million tenge)	 1,552		1,610</p>
<p> Sold (nominal, million tenge)	 604		  517</p>
<p> Average price			 97.41 pct	  97.49</p>
<p> Average yield			 10.64 pct	  10.30</p>
<p> Tenor				   91 days	    91 days</p>
<p> Maturity				Sept 18, 1997     Sept 4, 1997</p>
<p>--Almaty Newsroom, +7 3272 509410</p>
</text>
